{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["וַנֵּרָם — and we cast them from their place. And we destroy them. Just as from נטה it says וַנֵּט; so from ירה it says וַנִּיר. וְנִירָם — like ונרם. And so יַבְדִּילֵנִי from יבדלנו. לְהוֹצִיאָנוּ with qamatz, like לְהוֹצִיאֵנוּ with ṣere." "וַנִּשִּׂים — a vav-conversive form, and so too וַנִּירָם. And had it been explicit as in the Targum, it would have had to be pointed וְנִירָם with vav ḥaṭef."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The grammatical examples appear to address different vowel patterns: וַנֵּרָם with ṣere vs. וְנִירָם with ḥiriq; the final example compares qamatz vs. ṣere in pronominal suffixes.", 1 "Rashbam refers to the Targum's rendering of this verse (Onkelos: וְנַחְרִיבְהוֹן), which would require a different vocalization of ונירם (construct form with ḥaṭef on the vav) if the text matched the Aramaic explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:46.989472829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}